// Prototype classes: placeholder values, to balance with mass simulations.
// ClassId(i) is the i-th class of this list. A class's key names it in the language
// files (assets/lang, class-<key>); a spell's name is the fight logs' alone.
// reach: meters between the fighters' edges. power: % of the damage formula.
// cooldown: ticks, 30 per second. mana_per_second, endurance_per_second: recovered
// each second of a fight, up to the max.
// cost: what a cast spends, all of it needed (mana, endurance, elements of the floor
// from the fighter's reserve); what is left out costs nothing.
// max_elements: elements of the floor a fighter carries at most, 0 if left out. A spell's
// gathers adds that many of the arena's element (data/combat.ron) to its caster's
// reserve, without target nor damage; its thrown gives, for each element, the power,
// damage_kind and accuracy_drop it hits with in an arena of that element.
// mine: true lays a mine at the target's feet instead of hitting it; it blasts with the
// spell's power and damage_kind (mines in data/combat.ron). False if left out; a
// loadout's mines_per_cast (1 if left out) sets how many mines its mine spells lay.
// blows: a cast's blows, landing all or none on one hit roll, each with the spell's
// damage on its own part; 1 if left out.
// damage_kind: Blunt stuns three times as often as Cutting, which may sever a limb or
// the head instead (data/combat.ron); Neutral (spells without an element yet) does neither.
// spells: the first and third slots. Each of the class's two loadouts brings the second
// (spell), its weapon (a key of weapons in data/combat.ron, whose auto attack the fighter
// strikes with once none of its spells is both affordable and of use) and what its off
// hand holds: Free,
// Shield (a defense bonus) or Weapon (a second one, weaker for who is not ambidextrous;
// equipment in data/fighter.ron). A loadout's key names it in the language files
// (loadout-<key>).
